    "prompt": "Explain service desk purpose in Service Desk Foundations and User Experience. Which user or service outcome should it protect?",
    "preferred_answer": "The service desk is the central point of contact that connects users with the service provider and restores access to value. A strong response connects the concept to the support outcome, then explains that the operator should capture context, communicate clearly, own or coordinate the case, and confirm the user outcome. Evidence should include user impact, contact history, agreed next update and closure confirmation. It should explicitly avoid treating the desk as a ticket-routing queue rather than a relationship and recovery function.",
