    "prompt": "What is incident versus service request, and what evidence would help you recognise it correctly in a live support case?",
    "preferred_answer": "An incident is an unplanned interruption or reduction in quality; a service request is a predefined user need such as access, information or a standard fulfilment. Recognition should not rely on the ticket label alone. The analyst should collect symptoms, affected service, catalogue item, entitlement and workflow history, compare the observation with the expected service state, and then classify by outcome, apply the correct workflow and avoid hiding failures inside request queues. A key error is misclassification distorting SLA, prioritisation and problem data.",
