    "prompt": "A senior user asks the service desk to bypass normal controls to resolve an urgent issue involving end-to-end ownership. What do you do?",
    "preferred_answer": "Acknowledge urgency but do not equate seniority with authorisation. Establish the business impact and minimum safe outcome: Ownership means remaining accountable for progress and communication even when another team performs the technical work. Collect assignment trail, update cadence, dependency owner and user confirmation; choose the lowest-risk reversible action; and coordinate handoffs, maintain updates, challenge stalled queues and validate restoration. If an exception is still required, obtain the authorised owner, scope, expiry, monitoring and rollback. Refuse or escalate any request that would create ticket ping-pong and silent transfers.",
